[32m+[m[32m## Learning & Growth Management[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] **Learning navigation and views:** Add a separate protected Learning navigation item using a GraduationCap or BookOpen icon, following existing admin routing. Provide Overview, All Learning, Calendar, My Reflections, Skills Growth, Certificates and Analytics pages/views. Keep Learning independent of Hackathons, Projects, Experiences and Career Opportunities; provide responsive search, filtering, sorting and pagination where appropriate.[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] **Learning registration and lifecycle:** Administrator can register an experience with required program title and category; organizer/institution, description, official website, registration URL and source URL; participation mode (physical/in-person, online/virtual or hybrid), country, city, venue, meeting URL, start/end dates, deadline and timezone; motivation, expected outcomes, skills to acquire, goals and priority; free/paid, fee, scholarship/sponsorship and optional other expenses. Include Courses, Workshops, Summer Programs/Campaigns, Conferences, Meetups, Seminars, Webinars, Bootcamps, Mentorship Programs, Professional Meetings, Networking Events and Other Learning Experiences, and allow custom categories. Support INTERESTED, APPLIED, REGISTERED, CONFIRMED, IN_PROGRESS, COMPLETED, CANCELLED, REJECTED and DID_NOT_ATTEND; status changes preserve history. Completed status enables a separate reflection workflow; reflection completion is tracked independently from participation status.[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] **Learning reflections, skills and attachments:** Administrator can create/edit/save reflection drafts for completed experiences with what was learned, technical knowledge, soft skills, takeaways, challenges, people met, ideas/opportunities, application plan, action items, personal assessment/rating and additional notes. Track acquired skills across experiences; display certificates and other supporting materials. Registration confirmations, agendas, documents, certificates and photographs can be referenced as attachments. Preserve personal reflection text distinctly from optional AI suggestions.[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] **Learning dashboard and analytics:** Show total registered, completed, upcoming and active experiences; total learning hours only where recorded; skills acquired, completed reflections and certificates collected. Include upcoming programs, recently completed experiences, recent reflections, activity timeline and progress analytics. All totals/analytics derive only from stored records; do not invent sample data or fabricated statistics. Calendar displays upcoming stored programs.[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] **Optional AI Learning Companion:** Integrate the existing central AI assistant optionally for summarizing reflections, extracting acquired skills, identifying knowledge gaps, generating action plans, recommending relevant next learning opportunities, connecting experiences to portfolio projects, identifying recurring themes, and generating monthly/yearly learning reports. AI must not fabricate learning achievements or personal experiences; generated insights remain editable, visibly AI-generated and separate from personal reflections.[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] **Learning data security and integrity:** Use a normalized data model for learning experiences, reflections, skills, attachments and status history where appropriate. Implement admin-only CRUD; validate all inputs on the server; preserve relational integrity; reuse existing storage where available; avoid duplicating other admin modules or interfering with existing features. Verify new routes, schema and API behavior without mutating the shared managed database.[m
